t8.30am–8.30pm\\",\\n\\"Saturday 8.30am–8.30pm\\",\\n\\"Sunday\\t8.30am–8.30pm\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"priceRange\\": \\"INR\\",\\n  \\n  \\"telephone\\": \\" +91 8595321652, +91 7668527335\\",\\n  \\"url\\": \\"https://www.krphysiotherapy.com/\\"\\n}",{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can physiotherapists help with back pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes physiotherapists can manage back pain with best treatment plan. We do assessment to know the cause of back pain and we will plan treatment plan accordingly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best doctor to see for back pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If you have back pain you can directly consult to good physiotherapist and get the best physiotherapist at the centre or nursing homes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can back pain lead to any complications?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes untreated back pain lead to complications like sciatica, disability and other psychological disorder like depression, insomnia."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is dry needling useful in the treatment of back pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dry needling is effective in back pain to reduce muscle spasm and increase blood flow to promote the healing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is cupping therapy useful in treating back pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Doing cupping therapy is really good for back pain from trained therapist. It is very safe therapy to reduce back pain faster."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is sciatica same as back pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Back pain and sciatica is not the same. Back pain is olways feels at spine area but sciatica pain goes to down to the leg and foot beacause pressing of nerve roots of sciatica as in disc prolapse."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there different treatment options for upper and lower back pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes! Manual techaniques are different for upper and lower back pain."}}]}]', '2026-09-12 11:45:44', '2026-09-12 11:45:44');
