hursday 8.30am–8.30pm\\",\\n\\"Friday\\t8.30am–8.30pm\\",\\n\\"Saturday 8.30am–8.30pm\\",\\n\\"Sunday\\t8.30am–8.30pm\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"priceRange\\": \\"INR\\",\\n  \\n  \\"telephone\\": \\" +91 8595321652, +91 7668527335\\",\\n  \\"url\\": \\"https://www.krphysiotherapy.com/\\"\\n}",{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is physiotherapy good for shoulder pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes! Physiotherapy is good for shoulder pain. Using manual techniques, stretching, theraband exercises, dry needling, cupping therapy can relief from shoulder pain and prevent from further injury."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best therapy for shoulder pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Studies shows that physiotherapy modalities such as us, tens, ift, swd are best for reducing pain. Using monotherapy or comined with other manual therapy you can get relief from shiulder pain."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the physiotherapy exercises for shoulder pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Shoulder pain can be treated by stretching and range of motion exercises as prescribed by physiotherapist such as pendular movement, shoulder rolls, wall climbs, pendular movement, child’s pose can get rid of your shoulder pain"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you do shoulder physiotherapy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our expert physiotherapists have great knowledge for dealing with the shoulder pain. Electrotherapy and manual therapy are most often used in physiotherapy for shoulder pain. We are also expert in postural taping, cupping therapy & dry needling for instant relief."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How should I sleep with shoulder pain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If you are suffering from shoulder pain then you should avoid sleeping on affected side. The best position for sleeping is lying on back to promote healing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I stop my shoulder from hurting when I sleep?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Utilizing right mattress and pillow while sleeping can avoid the shoulder pain. Sleeping on non- affected side or back is more beneficial for shoulder pain."}}]}]', '2026-09-12 11:45:44', '2026-09-12 11:45:44');
